&lt;h2&gt;Why Marketers Are Switching from Marketo Now&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Adobe Marketo Engage is a powerful B2B marketing automation platform built for enterprise-scale demand generation. It supports lead nurturing, email marketing, account-based marketing (ABM), revenue attribution, and CRM integration. It’s been a category standard for over a decade.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Primary buyers of Marketo alternatives include B2B marketing leaders, RevOps leaders, and agency principals. So why are teams leaving? There are a few reasons:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;1. High Total Cost of Ownership&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketo’s licensing fees are just the starting point. The total cost of ownership includes license fees, services, admin time, integrations, training, and add-ons. Factor in implementation services, and the real cost of running Marketo often comes as a surprise.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;2. Steep Learning Curves and Admin Dependency&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketo is not a platform most marketers can run independently. Many organizations end up relying on a Marketo-certified admin or a consulting firm just to build campaigns and maintain workflows. That dependency slows execution and adds to operational cost.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;3. Fragmented Data Between Marketing and Sales&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketo integrates with Salesforce, but “integrates with” is not the same as “unified with.” Many teams report data sync delays, inconsistent lead records, and friction in the handoff between the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/how-to-build-a-marketing-stack"&gt;marketing stack&lt;/a&gt; and CRM — exactly the problems a modern revenue team can’t afford.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;4. Slow Time to Value&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Implementation timelines for Marketo routinely run three to six months before teams are fully operational. That window is too long for companies that need pipeline yesterday.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Platforms like &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing"&gt;Marketing Hub&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/crm/ai-crm"&gt;Smart CRM&lt;/a&gt; address each of these gaps. HubSpot’s tools have a unified architecture that connects marketing automation and CRM in one system, a visual workflow builder that doesn’t require technical expertise, and onboarding timelines measured in weeks, not quarters.&lt;/p&gt; 
